Offer Description
We are seeking for an experienced accountant to join our team. In this role, you will be reporting to the Chief Administrative Officer of the Consortium, the successful candidate will be responsible for the following main activities:
support the implementation of the new accounting software Ad Hoc revolution web;
ensure financial accuracy and compliance while tracking the financial data through detailed records and reports;
reconciling general ledgers and bank statements;
support the preparation of the financial statements for management, and tax reporting;
ensuring compliance with local, provincial and national regulations;
support the forecasting cash flow;
maintaining and updating CERIC budget and bookkeeping records;
support the financial reporting of all the funded and internal projects of CERIC-ERIC, according to the funding agency's policies, internal procedures and rules of CERIC.
Where to apply
E-mail: hr@ceric-eric.eu
Requirements
Research Field: Economics
Education Level: Bachelor Degree or equivalent
Skills/Qualifications:
University degree in Economics, Accounting or equivalent.
Experience in accounting for a minimum period of 8 years.
Good knowledge of the accounting software Zucchetti "Ad Hoc" or "Ad hoc revolution web".
Good knowledge of the Italian fiscal rules.
Good knowledge of English (minimum B2 level), both written and spoken.
Excellent knowledge of MS Office Suite.
Competences considered a plus:
Eager to help others;
Friendly, cheerful, positive and self-driven;
Strong work ethic;
Keen to learn, adapt and apply to new challenges;
Able to work independently and as part of a team;
Highly organized, comfortable with multi-tasking and with good attention to detail;
Excellent interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to communicate with colleagues across divisions and seniority;
Knowledge of additional languages of the Consortium is an advantage.
Additional Information
Benefits:
12 months Fixed – term contract, with the possibility of extension;
Possibility to work partially remotely;
Salary range from 32.000 € – to 38.000 € annually, will be commensurate with previous experience and qualifications of the candidates.
Bonus based on performance.
Benefits: 33 days of holidays per year, flexible working time, meal vouchers;
Training possibilities.
Selection process
How to apply: To apply for this job, please send your CV and a motivation letter to hr@ceric-eric.eu, with the following subject: Accounting officer.
For more information about the role, please contact: administation@ceric-eri.eu.
Deadline for application: July 24, 2026.
Additional comments
About CERIC: The Consortium was set up with the European Commission’s decision on June 2014, (214/392/EU) and its Statute was published in 26/6/2014 in the EU official Gazette. CERIC provides open access to some of the most advanced analytical facilities in Europe to help science and industry advance in all fields of materials, biomaterials and nanotechnology.
